  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nAn upper level trough is currently over the eastern Great Lakes\nthis morning. Scattered lake effect rain showers will be around\ntoday into this evening, mainly impacting the Snowbelt region of\nnortheast Ohio and northwest Pennsylvania. High temperatures\nwill range from the upper 40s to lower 50s. Skies will start to\nclear from the west to east late tonight into early Sunday\nmorning. Temperatures will drop tonight into the 30s away from \nthe immediate lakeshore. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \nHigh pressure will start to build into the Ohio Valley Sunday\nand remain through mid week. Mainly dry and milder weather will\nbe expected for the first half of next week. Another upper \ntrough will dig south into the region later in the week. There\nis the potential for unsettled weather to return at some point \nlater next week and colder weather.",
